1409 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Illustration showing three dietary patterns: Mediterranean with fish and vegetables, MIND with nuts and wine, and Western with fast food. A scale indicates favorable to unfavorable scores, based on dietary inflammatory index. Three molecular structures depicted below are Vitamin C, Docosahexaenoic Acid \(DHA\), and Cholesterol. The dietary scale ranges from macroscale to microscale on the right side.) /K 1462 0 R /P 240 0 R /Pg 221 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
1410 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Diagram of a brain's neural network with labeled regions. Nodes are linked by lines, indicating connectivity between areas like Superior Frontal, Superior Parietal, Frontal Pole, Temporal Pole, Inferior Temporal, Lateral Occipital, and Fusiform. The brain regions are color-coded.) /K 1463 0 R /P 240 0 R /Pg 227 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
1411 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Diagram illustrating the progression from monomers and small oligomers to fibrils and plaques. Three stages: health, impairment, and degeneration, represented with neurons. The reactions show transitions involving probabilities and rates.) /K 1464 0 R /P 240 0 R /Pg 229 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
